==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|house warming}}
* {{l|en|house-warming}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} A [[party]] to celebrate moving into a new [[home]].
#* {{quote-book|year=1898|author={{w|Winston Churchill (novelist)|Winston Churchill}}
|title={{w|The Celebrity}}|chapter=5
|passage=In the eyes of Mr. Farquhar Fenelon Cooke the apotheosis of the Celebrity was complete. The people of Asquith were not only willing to attend the '''house-warming''', but had been worked up to the pitch of eagerness.}}
# The act of [[welcoming]] a person/family to their [[new]]ly purchased or newly rented [[home]].
#: ''A '''housewarming''' gift.''
#* {{quote-journal|year=2004|volume=89|issue=4|page=580|title=Gadney's Immunity|author=Jacob M Appel|journal=Southwest Review|passage=They had their first argument on the evening Gadney moved in, their '''housewarming''' spat, he later called it.}}
#* {{quote-book|year=2011|title=The Offering|author=John Kinsella|passage=Fortunately, Dave had left them a packet of rollie tobacco and papers for a '''housewarming'''}}

